WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Café operator>Thanks for joining. This is the design session for CAFE-2026-002, the desk booking assistant.</v>

2
00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:25.000
<v Person 2>Our problem is simple: nobody can see which desks are free, so people email the floor team.</v>

3
00:01:30.000 --> 00:02:10.000
<v Person 3>As sponsor I want it live for two floors first. We would need it to read the Service Catalogue to find the desk inventory.</v>

4
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:55.000
<v Café operator>Understood. What would the assistant do on a single request?</v>

5
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:40.000
<v Person 9>It would take a date and a floor, check availability, and propose three desks. I would build that in Copilot Studio.</v>

6
00:03:45.000 --> 00:04:25.000
<v Person 2>It should also let people cancel a booking without emailing anyone.</v>

7
00:04:30.000 --> 00:05:10.000
<v Café operator>Good. Do you need any analysis of past usage to decide how many desks to hold back?</v>

8
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:55.000
<v Person 9>Yes, we could use Dataiku to look at the last six months of booking counts, using aggregated numbers only.</v>

9
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:40.000
<v Person 3>Keep it to aggregated figures. We cannot share anything that identifies who sat where.</v>

10
00:06:45.000 --> 00:07:25.000
<v Café operator>Agreed. Let us pick a feature list: availability search, desk proposals, cancellation, and a weekly utilisation summary.</v>

11
00:07:30.000 --> 00:08:10.000
<v Person 2>The weekly summary can wait. Availability and cancellation are the must-haves.</v>

12
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:55.000
<v Café operator>Great. Next step is for Person 9 to sketch the flow in Copilot Studio and bring it to the next session.</v>
